@*
    The compliance concern: a read-only audit of every current value in the tree
    against its enforcement policy. It never rewrites or dead-letters data, so it
    is gated on its own scoped decision (compliance.scan) rather than on the
    policy-management one.

    The non-compliant breakdown is the area's widest data surface, so it renders
    through the design system's adaptive table: a real table at medium and
    expanded, and a card list at compact, from one column declaration and with no
    media query of its own (epic decision D7).
*@

<div class="lx-schema-advanced">
    <h3 class="lx-schema-title">Compliance</h3>
    <p class="lx-schema-note">A read-only scan of every current value against this policy. It never rewrites or dead-letters data.</p>
    <button type="button" class="lx-schema-btn"
            disabled="@(!Session.Can(SchemaCapability.ScanCompliance))"
            @onclick="ScanAsync">Scan compliance</button>
    @if (_view is { } view)
    {
        @if (!view.IsSuccess)
        {
            <p class="lx-schema-result @SchemaStatusStyles.For(view.Status)" role="status">@view.Message</p>
        }
        else if (!view.Value.HasPolicy)
        {
            <p class="lx-schema-empty">Tree '@view.Value.TreeId' is ungoverned (no policy).</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <p class="lx-schema-compliant">Compliant: @view.Value.CompliantCount</p>
            <p class="lx-schema-noncompliant">Non-compliant: @view.Value.NonCompliantCount</p>
            <p class="lx-schema-sub">Scanned: @view.Value.ScannedCount</p>
            @if (view.Value.RuleBreakdown.Count > 0)
            {
                <h4 class="lx-schema-subtitle">Breakdown by reason</h4>
                <LatticeAdaptiveTable TItem="LatticeSchemaComplianceRuleCount"
                                      Items="view.Value.RuleBreakdown"
                                      Columns="BreakdownColumns"
                                      KeySelector="RowKey"
                                      Label="Non-compliance breakdown by reason" />
            }
        }
    }
</div>
